1
00:07:03,157 --> 00:07:09,157
He had the life expectancy of a match.

2
00:14:06,315 --> 00:14:12,315
The Key is a drama, romance, war film directed by Carol Reed.

3
00:21:09,473 --> 00:21:15,473
In wartime England, circa 1941, poorly-armed tugs are sent into
"U-Boat Alley" to rescue damaged Allied ships.

4
00:28:12,631 --> 00:28:18,631
An American named David Ross arrives to captain one of these tugs.

5
00:35:15,789 --> 00:35:21,789
He's given a key by a fellow tugboat-man -- a key to an
apartment and its pretty female resident.

6
00:42:18,947 --> 00:42:24,947
Should something happen to the friend, Ross can use the key.

7
00:49:22,105 --> 00:49:28,105
Capt. David Ross, played by William Holden.

8
00:56:25,263 --> 00:56:31,263
Stella, played by Sophia Loren.

9
01:03:28,421 --> 01:03:34,421
Capt. Chris Ford, played by Trevor Howard.

10
01:10:31,578 --> 01:10:37,578
Cmdr. Wadlow, played by Bernard Lee.

11
01:17:34,736 --> 01:17:40,736
Van Dam, played by Oskar Homolka.

12
01:24:37,894 --> 01:24:43,894
Kane, played by Kieron Moore.

13
01:31:41,052 --> 01:31:47,052
The Key is a 1958 British-American war film set in
1941 during the Battle of the Atlantic.

14
01:38:44,210 --> 01:38:50,210
It was based on the 1951 novel Stella by Jan de Hartog (later republished as
The Distant Shore and The Key) and was directed by Carol Reed.

15
01:45:47,368 --> 01:45:53,368
William Holden, Sophia Loren and Trevor Howard starred in the production.

16
01:52:50,526 --> 01:52:56,526
The key to a flat in wartime Britain may augur bad luck for a succession of tug captains of the Royal Navy whose task is to rescue crippled ships in "U-boat
Alley." As each takes possession from his unfortunate predecessor, the flat's other occupant, a Swiss expatriate named Stella, apparently comes with it.

17
01:59:53,684 --> 01:59:59,684
The latest captain struggles with his conflicting fears
and affection for its apparent jinx.

18
02:06:56,842 --> 02:07:02,842
The tone is emotional.
